  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649018",
      "title": "Setting HTML Attributes Dynamically & Loading Image Files",
      "sourceHash": "bc72afa65d940306e3dfbcb57c02670d0850b32bde3e223e6ca19d9c5a3ab24e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 1.86,
          "en": "So now that we learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.86,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "outputting dynamic values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "with this special curly brace syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 12.53,
          "en": "we can use that same syntax to load our images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 14.43,
          "en": "in a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.43,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "or to point at those images in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 21.39,
          "en": "Now of course, loading this image like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.39,
          "end": 24.06,
          "en": "and displaying it works fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.06,
          "end": 26.66,
          "en": "as you can tell by the fact that the image is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.57,
          "end": 31.2,
          "en": "But this is actually not the best way of loading it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 34.77,
          "en": "To be precise, this source attribute value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.77,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "is not the best way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 40.56,
          "en": "because here I'm pointing at the image in my SRC folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.56,
          "end": 42.81,
          "en": "and there at the assets folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.81,
          "end": 44.7,
          "en": "But by loading it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 47.07,
          "en": "the image might actually get lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.07,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "once we prepare this React project for deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "Now, deployment is something we'll take a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "later in the course, but as part of the deployment process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 61.56,
          "en": "your entire code will be transformed, optimized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 63.3,
          "en": "and bundled together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 67.68,
          "en": "And image files, when loaded like this, might be ignored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 70.38,
          "en": "by that bundling process and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "they might get lost during deployment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "In addition, if we include images differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 81.15,
          "en": "we can even take advantage of extra optimization steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 85.11,
          "en": "which we're not getting with this way of including them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.11,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "So how should you then load and include images?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "Well, you should use an import statement and you can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "for example, import the React image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "though this name here is totally up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 104.96000000000001,
          "en": "from, and then you create a relative path from that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.66,
          "end": 109.89,
          "en": "So from the app JSX file this case to the image file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.89,
          "end": 112.65,
          "en": "So in this case, I dive into the assets folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 117.65,
          "en": "and then there it's this React core concepts PNG file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.78,
          "end": 121.293,
          "en": "So I point at this file here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "And this approach might look rather strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 130.91,
          "en": "because importing an image file into a JavaScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "is not something you can normally do in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "But here this will work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "because of that same build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "that will also make JSX code work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 146.97,
          "en": "Basically, that build process will not just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.97,
          "end": 151.97,
          "en": "transform the JSX code, but also import statements like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 155.22,
          "en": "and also import statements like this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.22,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "in the index JSX file, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "where we import a CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 163.353,
          "en": "which also normally wouldn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.73,
          "end": 168.99,
          "en": "But such imports do work in this project set up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.99,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "because the build process will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "that the files we're importing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "will be included in the final page and deployment package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "And we can therefore use syntax like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "to then use this React image, which we're loading like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "as a value for this source attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 192.66,
          "en": "by using single curly braces again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.66,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "So by using this dynamic value syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 198.21,
          "en": "about which you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.21,
          "end": 201.93,
          "en": "Here the dynamic value for the source attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 201.93,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "is that image which we are importing like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 210.27,
          "en": "So here, this image in the end is a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "Or to be precise, it's a JavaScript variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.14,
          "en": "that will point at that image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.14,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "that will include a path to that image, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "And it's therefore that variable, which includes that path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 228.54,
          "en": "which we want to use as a value for this SRC attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 228.54,
          "end": 233.01,
          "en": "And this here is then the syntax for doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 233.01,
          "end": 236.04,
          "en": "What's really important here when using this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 236.04,
          "end": 240.24,
          "en": "dynamic value expression for attribute values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "is that you don't add quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 245.73,
          "en": "You must omit those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.73,
          "end": 248.7,
          "en": "Instead, you have the dynamic value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.7,
          "end": 251.489,
          "en": "this curly brace syntax here, as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.489,
          "end": 256.473,
          "en": "right after that equal sign not wrapped by quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.31,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "And with that you'll see that if you save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "and you reload, you still see that image here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 266.28,
          "en": "So that still works, but we're now loading it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.28,
          "end": 269.94,
          "en": "in a more optimal way, thanks to this build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.94,
          "end": 271.71,
          "en": "which is part of this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 274.77,
          "en": "and this single curly brace syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.77,
          "end": 279.77,
          "en": "which we can use in JSX to point at JavaScript values.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
